WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.369
The other day I was scrolling Twitter and saw indie developer Peter

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.503
Levels post a tweet.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.473
He said everyone around him is scrambling to make money,

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.843
buying up assets — stocks, ETFs, gold, real estate —

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:13.279
all with one goal: be well-positioned before AGI arrives.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.982
Honestly, I usually don't find this kind of talk convincing,

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.884
because it tends to feel like fear-mongering.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:18.685
But that day, after reading it,

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.120
I quietly hit that like button.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.321
Because I genuinely agree with him.

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.657
AI is driving a massive wealth transfer,

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.527
and those who see it clearly are already racing to stake their position.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:29.129
I know someone's going to say, "See? See?"

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.463
"You're just spreading anxiety too, aren't you?"

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.699
But those "don't worry, just focus on yourself,

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.300
everything will be fine" videos —

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.735
I actually think that's a form of dishonesty.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:36.803
It's like the early days of the Industrial Revolution —

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.039
telling workers about to be replaced by machines,

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.840
"Don't worry, just relax" —

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.642
nobody could actually relax.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.011
When the wave hits, you only have two choices:

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.280
face it head-on and figure out where you stand,

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.681
or bury your head in the sand

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:49.749
and pretend nothing is happening.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.717
And this race —

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.119
I believe you can't sit it out, whether you like it or not.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.822
So as an investor, how do you position yourself?

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.057
Today I want to talk through

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.126
the four dimensions of investing in the age of AI.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.196
But before we dive in —

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.565
I want to take 30 seconds to thank this channel's long-time

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.267
partner, Interactive Brokers.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.902
IB is an award-winning,

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.503
globally recognized brokerage

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.272
and the platform I personally use to invest in US stocks.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:13.740
I love it for mainly two reasons:

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.341
first, trading costs are extremely low —

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.710
commission-free in many regions, or

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.312
so minimal it barely matters.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:19.646
Second,

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.649
its FX conversion rates are very competitive. I buy US

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:22.849
stocks from Canada,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:24.717
so I'm constantly converting CAD to USD.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.120
Compared to Canadian brokers charging 1.5%+

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.621
in conversion fees,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:31.191
IB's FX fees are in a completely different league.

